NASA Technical Reports Server documents (aerospace durability, 2026-09-29)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Flight-exposure results for metals, read from NASA conference papers retrieved
from the NASA Technical Reports Server (ntrs.nasa.gov) on 2026-09-29. NTRS
recorded each as "GOV_PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED" or "PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED" with no
third-party material that day. Nothing from them is redistributed here: the PDFs,
the transcription and the row-level table live in gitignored
cache/external/aerospace/. reports/ may contain aggregates and values derived
from them, with the locator of each. Reuse implies no NASA endorsement, and the
NASA insignia is not reproduced.

  A. F. Whitaker, "Selected results for metals from LDEF experiment A0171",
  NASA conference paper, 1992. NTRS 19930001391.

  J. A. Vaughn, R. C. Linton, M. M. Finckenor, R. R. Kamenetzky, "Evaluation of
  space environmental effects on metals and optical thin films on EOIM-3", NASA
  conference paper, 1995. NTRS 19950021220.

  R. C. Linton, J. A. Vaughn, M. M. Finckenor, R. R. Kamenetzky, "Orbital atomic
  oxygen effects on materials: An overview of MSFC experiments on the STS-46
  EOIM-3", NASA conference paper, 1995. NTRS 19950021216.

Six further NTRS documents were read on 2026-10-08 (UTC) under the same terms and with the
same handling (NTRS licence fields: GOV_PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED, except PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED for
the MISSE 6 presentation; no third-party material):

  A. de Rooij, "Some results of the oxidation investigation of copper and silver
  samples flown on LDEF", LDEF Materials Workshop 1991, Part 2, NASA LaRC, 1992.
  NTRS 19930001392.

  G. N. Raikar, J. C. Gregory, L. C. Christl, P. N. Peters, "The interaction of
  atomic oxygen with copper: an XPS, AES, XRD, optical transmission and stylus
  profilometry study", LDEF - 69 Months in Space, Part 3: Second Post-Retrieval
  Symposium, NASA LaRC, 1993. NTRS 19930019095. (NTRS 19930011567, NASA CR-192306,
  encloses a copy and was checked, not ingested.)

  J. C. Gregory, "Results from LDEF experiment A0114: the interaction of atomic oxygen
  with materials surfaces at orbital altitudes", NASA CR-196016, 1994. NTRS 19940030882.

  T. L. Morton, D. C. Ferguson, "Atomic oxygen exposure of power system and other
  spacecraft materials: results of the EOIM-3 experiment", NASA TM-107427, 1997.
  NTRS 19970025577.

  M. M. Finckenor, J. L. Golden, M. Kravchenko, M. J. O'Rourke, "Analysis of
  International Space Station vehicle materials on MISSE 6", National Space & Missile
  Materials Symposium, 2010. NTRS 20100033233.

  D. Burns, M. Finckenor, B. Henrie, "MISSE in the Materials and Processes Technical
